    "body": "\r\n> the thing I'm not sure about how to best define is the `select:not(:listbox)` thing. Any pointers?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSince adding a pseudo-class for listbox vs dropdown select elements [didn't work out](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7422#issuecomment-3113959029), we just reference the [drop-down box](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#drop-down-box) definition explicitly with prose like this example in the rendering section:\r\n\r\n> The following styles are [expected](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#expected) to apply to [select](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-select-element) elements when they are being rendered as a [drop-down box](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#drop-down-box) with [native appearance](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ui/#native-appearance) or [primitive appearance](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ui/#primitive-appearance):\r\n> \r\n> ```css\r\n> @namespace \"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\";\r\n> \r\n> select {\r\n>   display: inline-block;\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
